<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashraf Ghani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashraf Ghani is an Afghan academic and politician who served as president of the Islamic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> from 2014 to 2021, at first sharing power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-abdullah">Abdullah Abdullah</a>. As the Taliban took the country following the US withdrawal, he fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> on 15 August 2021, and the republic collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashraf-ghani.jpg" alt="Ashraf Ghani" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original author: Mueller /MSC · CC BY 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aschraf_Ghani_MSC_2017_2_(cropped)_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
